From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:38:11 +0300
Subject: OpenGL: apply the sprite recolour in the GLSL 1.10 sprite shader

The GLSL 1.10 sprite fragment shader looked up the palette with the
sprite's own index instead of the recoloured one, so recoloured sprites
drawn by the OpenGL backend (mouse cursors in company colours) kept
their original colours on drivers without GLSL 1.50. The GLSL 1.50
shader already uses the recoloured index.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/table/opengl_shader.h b/src/table/opengl_shader.h
--- a/src/table/opengl_shader.h
+++ b/src/table/opengl_shader.h
@@ -175,7 +175,7 @@ static const char *_frag_shader_sprite_blend[] = {
 	"void main() {",
 	"  float idx = texture2DLod(remap_tex, colour_tex_uv, zoom).r;",
 	"  float r = texture1D(pal, idx).r;",
-	"  vec4 remap_col = texture1D(palette, idx);",
+	"  vec4 remap_col = texture1D(palette, r);",
 	"  vec4 rgb_col = texture2DLod(colour_tex, colour_tex_uv, zoom);",
 	"",
 	"  if (crash && idx == 0.0) rgb_col.rgb = vec2(dot(rgb_col.rgb, vec3(0.199325561523, 0.391342163085, 0.076004028320)), 0.0).rrr;"
